Proposed Flow

“Start Your Protocol” CTA

Launch a full-screen multi-step wizard instead of jumping straight to a single page.
Steps:
Goal & Focus Quiz – capture objectives (sleep, focus, body recomposition), constraints (time, schedule), preferences (morning vs evening routines).
Context – ask about current habits, experience level, available equipment.
Motivation & Nudges – short science-backed blurbs for each goal so users understand why it matters.
Summary – show immediate tailored protocol (morning/night anchors, recommended reading). Prompt: “Save & Track this plan”.
Account Prompt

If the user wants to save, present a lightweight auth dialog (social sign-in + email).
Clarify benefits: saved protocols, adaptive adjustments, streaks, digests.


    3. Dashboard Experience (post-login)

Focus Areas – highlight active goals, show most relevant protocols with evidence snippets.
Streaks & Progress – daily completion toggles, weekly stats, gentle streak nudges (“You’ve kept your morning light routine 4 days in a row—here’s what that means.”).
Progress Tracking – allow users to rate adherence or subjective metrics (sleep quality, energy, focus). Display trends/percent improvements with research-based context.
Goals Tab – include short, science-backed blurbs per goal: “Why this matters”, “How long to see change”.
Action Digests – weekly or monthly emails summarizing adherence, streaks, and suggested next steps.

    4. Personalized Reminders

Offer optional calendar sync or push notifications that mirror the tailored protocol (morning light reminder, evening dimming cue, NSDR session prompt).

    5. Future Enhancements

Gamification: badges for consistency (e.g., “Circadian Champion” after 14 days).
Community/social proof: share progress graphs anonymously or invite accountability partners.
Adaptive content: adjust recommendations based on logged adherence or feedback (lightening the plan if overwhelmed, suggesting advanced protocols if streaks are high).
Implementation Notes

Start with a client-side wizard storing quiz inputs; wire it to your existing data structures (protocol arrays) to assemble personalized plans.
When auth arrives, persist quiz results, tailored protocols, and tracking data in a backend (Supabase / Firebase / Next API routes + DB).
The dashboard can be a new route (/dashboard) using server components fed by the saved user profile.
Carefully scope the first release: quiz → summary → optional save → minimal dashboard with streak counter + protocol list. Layer advanced analytics, digests, and gamification progressively.
Happy to help wire up the wizard or prototype the dashboard structure next.